# Reflection - Unit 1: Your First Android App

## What I Learned
- How to write simple Kotlin programs that display text output.
- How to install and configure Android Studio for development.
- How to build a basic layout with text and images using XML.
- How to run an app on an emulator or physical device.

## Challenges
- Setting up the Android Studio environment and emulator took time.
- Understanding the structure of XML layouts was initially confusing.
- Linking Kotlin code with UI components required practice.

## My Choices
- I used a LinearLayout for simplicity in arranging text and images.
- I added a custom image to personalize the app interface.
- I chose Kotlin as the language to align with modern Android development practices.

## Outcome
Completing Unit 1 gave me confidence in setting up Android Studio, writing Kotlin code, and designing simple user interfaces. This unit laid the foundation for future labs by combining language basics with Android SDK principles.
